    description: "SwiftUI is a system framework: apps import it and declare no package dependency, and 'import SwiftUI' does not trigger the YAML. So the App, app-delegate and ParsableCommand rows (swiftui.yaml:20, :24, :28, :52, :54 at 89e5af4c1) fire only on a fixture that names the dependency. The audit measured 0 of 4,756 nodes on swift-argument-parser. Repro: fixtures/rows/swift (no entry) vs fixtures/rows/swiftui (entries). Also: ParsableCommand belongs to swift-argument-parser, not SwiftUI; its rows sit in the wrong file.\n\nEvidence: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_build_11172026/pr7/fasij/RESULTS.md. Found while building the entry-kind PR (2026-11-21)."  # 26c1
