  message: "DONE in PR #2329. swiftui.yaml now loads where production Swift code imports SwiftUI, UIKit or AppKit (profile.py, a separate set _IMPORT_IS_THE_EVIDENCE_FRAMEWORKS: frameworks whose import is the only evidence a repository can carry; the promotion keeps its production-importer and Swift-import gates). The ParsableCommand rows moved to swift-argument-parser.yaml (detected from the Package.swift dependency or a production import of ArgumentParser). The XCTestCase row moved to test-frameworks.yaml: XCTest is only imported by tests, so no framework file keyed on it would load.\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE (dev a5b3cca93 vs the branch): swift-composable-architecture/Examples (100 files import SwiftUI): frameworks [] to [swiftui]; 11 entrypoint concepts (8 App conformers, 3 app delegates) and 11 main_function entries, from 0. swift-argument-parser, the repo the audit measured at 0 of 4,756 nodes: frameworks [] to [swift-argument-parser]; 240 command concepts and 20 cli_command entries, from 0. No node, edge or id change on either. 5 of 5 mutations red.\nWRONG IN THE RESULT: 1 of the 240 is the protocol AsyncParsableCommand itself (it refines ParsableCommand). Filed.\nNOT DONE: Swift's test* method rows match nothing (part of the 18-row item filed from WI-lunal). An Xcode project's own package declarations are still not read.\nEvidence: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/three_pr_plan_11222026/pr2/RESULTS.md.\n\nFILED FROM THIS: WI-jilid (the protocol stamped a command); the Swift test rows are in WI-rasok."  # cccb
